                <pb facs="0811" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg799"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/27258: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-19T23:00:00-04:00">January 19, 1943—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 20—12:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. Following Foreign Minister Fernández’s exposition of Chilean foreign policy
                    before the Senate this body at 9 p.m. today voted 30 for, 10 against, with 2
                    abstentions, its approval of “policy adopted by the President of the Republic
                    who, in exercise of his constitutional prerogatives, has announced his decision
                    to break relations of Chile with the Axis Governments”. No official statement
                    has yet been issued by the Government in this connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
